{"name":"Geranium","hex":"#dc465d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Geranium","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Geraniaceae – cranesbills; formerly including storksbills now classified as Pelargonium and Erodium."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Geranium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geranium","blocks":[{"text":"Geranium is a genus of 422 species of annual, biennial, and perennial plants that are commonly known as geraniums, hardy geraniums, or cranesbills. They are found throughout the temperate regions of the world and the mountains of the tropics, with the greatest diversity in the eastern part of the Mediterranean region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg/330px-Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geranium","wikidata":"Q157211"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg/500px-Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg/500px-Geranium_sanguineum02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"bill\" and seed dispersal mechanism of G. pratense","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeranium_sanguineum02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/500px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg/1280px-Geranium_%28probably_%27Johnson%27s_Blue%27%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser